EC2 vs Lightsail

| Feature                | **EC2**         | **Lightsail**            |
| ---------------------- | --------------- | ------------------------ |
| Complexity             | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ Higher     | ⭐ Easy                   |
| Control                | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ Very high | ⭐⭐⭐ Limited              |
| Configuration          | Very flexible   | Simplified               |
| Scaling                | Excellent       | Simpler                  |
| Networking             | Advanced        | Simplified               |
| Security configuration | Advanced        | Easier                   |
| Large applications     | ✅ Excellent     | ⚠️ Limited               |
| Small websites         | ✅               | ✅ Excellent              |
| Beginner friendly      | ⚠️              | ✅                        |
| ML workloads           | ✅ Good          | ⚠️ Usually not preferred |
| Enterprise workloads   | ✅               | ⚠️                       |
| Simple website         | Maybe overkill  | ✅ Good                   |


=====

Simple real-world example

Imagine you want to open a restaurant.

Lightsail 🍽️

You rent a ready-made small restaurant.

AWS Lightsail
     ↓
Ready server
     ↓
Install website
     ↓
Run

Easy to start, fewer decisions.

EC2 🏢

You rent an empty commercial building.

You decide:

CPU
RAM
Storage
Network
Security
Operating System
Firewall
Scaling
Load Balancer
Monitoring

Much more control, but more responsibility.

=====


When would you choose each?

Choose EC2 when:

"I need a highly customizable virtual server and I want to manage the application/server myself."

Choose Lightsail when:

"I need a simple, small server or website and I want easier setup."

Choose SageMaker when:

"I want AWS to provide ML-specific training, model deployment, and inference capabilities."

